--- body ---

## Context

Memory may suggest requirements but must not become another instruction system or decision ledger. Harvesting proposes changes through the normal adoption process. A particular lesson can warrant a harvest directly: candidate grouping, synthesis and model integration are not prerequisites.

Design baseline: v6, merged by PR #903. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Dreaming/memory skills; existing rules and hook workflows; canonical project decision records; library relationship metadata.

## Actions

1. Identify lessons that justify a rule, procedure or mechanically enforceable invariant, without requiring a proposal on each run.
2. Create reviewable proposals in the existing workflow; adopted decisions stay in their established canonical records.
3. After acceptance, preserve incident evidence and link the governing artefact. Qualify obsolete copied prescriptions so they cannot compete with its newer procedure.
4. Use normal licence assessment for any reused component and ordinary review for hook/rule changes; no auto-adoption via memory score.

## Test

Scenario with a harvested procedure later amended: discovery points to current canonical advice and preserved memory is qualified as historical evidence. Proposal without approval does not become an instruction.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v6, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Harvesting has a no-change outcome and no mandatory residency class.
- [ ] Existing governance and knowledge-hint interfaces reused.
- [ ] Evidence preserved without duplicating decisions or authoritative procedures.
